From: PS3 Custom Toolchain
Subject: [PATCH] vect: no optimized realignment for an ungrouped load with a vectorization factor below the lane count

vect_supportable_dr_alignment chose dr_explicit_realign_optimized for an
access that is not grouped without checking how far it moves per vector
iteration; the step check only ran for grouped accesses.  With every loop
statement vectorised through SLP, an ungrouped single-lane load can now have
a vectorization factor of 1 below the lane count (a splat of rows[y] feeding
a 16-lane store group).  The realignment token is computed once in the
preheader, but the load advances one element per iteration, so every vector
after the first was permuted with the wrong mask: on the Cell PPU (AltiVec,
no VSX) rows 1 and 2 of tests/regression/vect-realign-splat read the zeroed
stack slot after the table, at -O3, in both data models.

Treat an ungrouped access as a group of one in the existing check, so such
a load is not realigned with one token; it falls back to the misalignment
support query (unsupported without VSX), and the vectorizer picks another
plan.  Upstream GCC 16.1 and trunk carry the same code.

Codegen cost, measured with Linux-hosted cc1 builds (base = 0001-0081,
candidate = +0082):
- v0.26.0 archives: all 22 translation units behind the 35 shipped functions
  that contain lvsr (SDK at -O2, both data models; cairo, freetype, pixman,
  libpng, tiny3d) compile to identical assembly; no shipped code changes.
- gcc.dg/vect, vect/costmodel/ppc and gcc.target/powerpc AltiVec tests
  (2312 that compile here), -mcpu=cell -maltivec: -O2 0 changed; -O3 5
  changed, 2583 -> 2435 instructions in those files, loops vectorized
  2015 -> 2015.  vect-62, vect-64 and no-section-anchors-vect-64 lose the
  bad realignment (vectorized with unroll factor 4 instead); bb-slp-phis-1
  and slp-58 change only an alias-check bound (same instruction count).
- vect_realign_fill (the regression witness): 84 -> 67 instructions under
  ILP32, 81 -> 67 under LP64.
---
diff --git a/gcc/tree-vect-data-refs.cc b/gcc/tree-vect-data-refs.cc
--- a/gcc/tree-vect-data-refs.cc
+++ b/gcc/tree-vect-data-refs.cc
@@ -6893,12 +6893,18 @@
 	      || targetm.vectorize.builtin_mask_for_load ()))
 	{
 	  /* If we are doing SLP then the accesses need not have the
-	     same alignment, instead it depends on the SLP group size.  */
+	     same alignment, instead it depends on the SLP group size.
+	     An access that is not grouped is a group of one: with a
+	     vectorization factor below the number of lanes (an SLP load
+	     with a load permutation) consecutive vector loads advance by
+	     less than a vector and their misalignment changes, so one
+	     realignment token cannot serve them all.  */
 	  if (loop_vinfo
-	      && STMT_VINFO_GROUPED_ACCESS (stmt_info)
 	      && !multiple_p (LOOP_VINFO_VECT_FACTOR (loop_vinfo)
-			      * (DR_GROUP_SIZE
-				   (DR_GROUP_FIRST_ELEMENT (stmt_info))),
+			      * (STMT_VINFO_GROUPED_ACCESS (stmt_info)
+				 ? DR_GROUP_SIZE
+				     (DR_GROUP_FIRST_ELEMENT (stmt_info))
+				 : 1),
 			      TYPE_VECTOR_SUBPARTS (vectype)))
 	    ;
 	  else if (!loop_vinfo
